      "eyebrow": "Sources",
      "heading": "Official sources",
      "html": "<p>For rented homes in England, the C1, C2, C3 and FI codes, the 28-day rule and the written confirmation come from the government guidance and the 2020 Regulations. The code definitions for other buildings, and the 10 and 5 year intervals, come from industry standards (BS 7671, IET Guidance Note 3) that are not linked here. Official sources checked on 18 November 2026.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/electrical-safety-standards-in-the-private-and-social-rented-sectors-guidance/electrical-safety-standards-in-the-private-and-social-rented-sectors-guidance\" rel=\"noopener\">Electrical safety standards in the private and social rented sectors: guidance (GOV.UK)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2020/312\" rel=\"noopener\">The Electrical Safety Standards in the Private Rented Sector and Social Rented Sector (England) Regulations 2020 (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li></ul>"
    },
